From f6c6adef9f17c513506f2a38a3d7f0a7134317f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Feng Zhang <feng@radxa.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:25:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(drm): retry HDMI DDC writes with the same byte

The DDC write loop advances both the data pointer and register address
before checking completion. On an I2C error, it restores only the
address and remaining length, so retries send the next byte and can read
past a short payload.

Rewind the data pointer together with the register address before
retrying. Preserve the existing retry count and error returns.

Signed-off-by: Feng Zhang <feng@radxa.com>
---
 drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_hdmi20/dw_i2cm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_hdmi20/dw_i2cm.c b/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_hdmi20/dw_i2cm.c
index 8a89d713..9aab3daa 100644
--- a/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_hdmi20/dw_i2cm.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_hdmi20/dw_i2cm.c
@@ -177,6 +177,7 @@ int _dw_i2cm_write(unsigned char *buf, unsigned int length)
 			hdmi_err("dw i2c write error, retry count: %d\n", retry_cnt);
 			if (retry_cnt) {
 				length++;
+				buf--;
 				i2cm->slave_reg--;
 				retry_cnt--;
 				continue;
